# The image builds from tracked sources only. Every .gitignore pattern is excluded here too, in
# Docker's form: Docker matches a pattern from the context root, git at any depth unless the pattern
# has an inner slash, so an unanchored git pattern `x` becomes `**/x` (container-config.test.ts
# checks it). The build context is then exactly the files git reports, and smoke evidence that names
# a clean commit really did build from that commit.
.git/
docs/
trace/
retro/
openspec/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/test-results-stack/
**/test-results-record/
**/playwright-report-stack/
**/*.log
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/uploads/
**/storage/
**/pgdata/
**/backups/
**/*.dump
**/raw/
src/api/generated/
docs/qa/full-demo/*.webm
docs/qa/full-demo/snaps/
docs/qa/full-demo/failure.png
